  "behavior": [
    "The actual BaseSequence is heap-stable canonical Arc storage. All structural edits use short mutation closures under the same mutex as const Value cache updates. No lock or metadata borrow crosses item Drop.",
    "Raw and typed indexed/range/cursor removal share native preparation routines. Index/range topology and cache update before Drop. Native cursor current advances before Drop; previous remains unchanged. Cursor-end removal remains no-op.",
    "Clear leaves actual original size/head/tail/cache available during every normal destructor, including opaque identities of already destroyed nodes; it nullifies metadata afterwards. A panic reset guard clears metadata before remaining ownership unwind.",
    "SequenceObserver returns one synchronized snapshot of canonical fields. The snapshot is not stored back or used as an authoritative mirror. Cache node/index are read as one consistent pair.",
    "SequenceNativeCursor owns observable canonical cursor state separately from the existing Copy SequenceCursor. Clone copies state independently. Forward/backward operations and removal resolve current ownership to original retained pointers before dereferencing, including arena address reuse.",
    "Moves transfer actual BaseSequence fields while leaving observer handles attached to their logical owner. Observer handles can safely outlive an emptied or destroyed owner.",
    "HashMap<usize, SequenceNodeOwner<T>> indexes allocation ownership only. Native links remain the only iteration/destruction order and per-node original allocators/provenance remain paired. Cursor value/change_value/next/previous use fresh indexed membership.",
    "Range panic cleanup releases the entire detached span in forward order; surviving native metadata already reflects the complete range deletion. This safe unwind completion is a Rust extension, not a claim about native throwing destructors."
  ],
