    "analysis": "Vec ownership lookup was linear per removal, with floor((n+1)^2/4) equality checks for append-order full clear. Address-keyed ownership removes that scan, giving expected O(1) removal ownership lookup. Canonical index/cache lookup complexity remains native. Indexed cursor membership changes ordinary full cursor traversal from O(n^2) to expected O(n).",
