  "remaining_gaps": [
    "Observer parity is bounded to readonly size/endpoints/cache and native cursor links; arbitrary destructor reentry into item reads, structural mutation or allocator extension callbacks is not claimed.",
    "SequenceBaseAccess retains the cache mutex and a shared native base reference. Same-thread Value/cache access or observer snapshot while holding that guard can deadlock; documented release-before-reentry restriction remains. This is not full native base-reference equivalence.",
    "Observable native cursor support covers construction/copy, next/previous, position and removal. Other observer-aware native editing overloads remain separate work.",
    "The Arc/Mutex, private ownership HashMap and range panic-cleanup owner Vec add Rust allocation/synchronization overhead. Native allocation footprint and full performance parity remain unclaimed.",
